# project: mobile-os-compat-update

VAR rejections = 0
VAR rollout_stage = 0

=== bump_sdk ===
Bump the target SDK and upgrade dependencies for the annual mobile OS compatibility update.
Done when the project builds against the new SDK with updated dependency versions.
* [SDK and dependencies bumped] -> fix_issues

=== fix_issues ===
Fix whatever the bump broke, plus any issues cycled back from regression or QA.
Done when known breakage is addressed and the build is ready for the regression suite.
+ [Fixes in, run the suite] -> regression_suite

=== regression_suite ===
Run the full regression suite against the new SDK build; repeat until green.
+ [Suite green] -> qa_exploratory
+ [Failures found] ~loop~ -> fix_issues

=== qa_exploratory ===
QA does an exploratory pass on the new OS beta build.
Issues found here cycle back to the fix stage.
+ [QA signs off, no blocking issues] @human -> submit_to_store
+ [Issues found] ~loop~ -> fix_issues

=== submit_to_store ===
Submit the compatibility build for store review.
+ [Store approved; release manager green-lights the 10% stage] @human -> rollout_10
+ [Store rejected the build] -> address_rejection

=== address_rejection ===
Address the store review feedback and prepare a resubmission.
~ rejections += 1
+ {rejections < 2} [Fixed, resubmit] ~loop~ -> submit_to_store
+ {rejections >= 2} [Two rejections: release manager weighs in before the next attempt] @human ~loop~ -> submit_to_store

=== rollout_10 ===
Staged rollout at 10% for a week, watching crash rates.
Any spike halts the rollout for a hotfix and the stage restarts.
~ rollout_stage = 10
+ [Week clean; release manager approves 50%] @human -> rollout_50
+ [Crash rate spike: halt the stage] -> hotfix

=== rollout_50 ===
Rollout expanded to 50%, still watching crash rates.
~ rollout_stage = 50
+ [Stable; release manager approves 100%] @human -> rollout_100
+ [Crash rate spike: halt the stage] -> hotfix

=== rollout_100 ===
Full rollout at 100%, monitored until stable.
~ rollout_stage = 100
+ [Rollout complete and stable] -> END
+ [Crash rate spike: halt] -> hotfix

=== hotfix ===
Rollout is halted; build and ship a hotfix, then restart the halted stage.
+ {rollout_stage == 10} [Hotfix out, restart the 10% stage] ~loop~ -> rollout_10
+ {rollout_stage == 50} [Hotfix out, restart the 50% stage] ~loop~ -> rollout_50
+ {rollout_stage == 100} [Hotfix out, restart the 100% stage] ~loop~ -> rollout_100
